# Legal Analysis & Statutory Interpretation Standard

## 1. Doctrinal Method
- Follow CJEU teleological interpretation: analyze the text in its grammatical meaning, legislative context, and overarching regulatory objective.
- For international treaties, adhere strictly to Articles 31 and 32 of the Vienna Convention on the Law of Treaties (VCLT):
  - General rule of interpretation (good faith, ordinary meaning in context, object and purpose).
  - Supplementary means of interpretation (travaux préparatoires and circumstances of conclusion).

## 2. EU AI Act Tiered Scrutiny Protocol
- **Tier 0 (Scope & Exclusions)**: Article 2 (National security, exclusive military use, pure scientific R&D, personal non-professional).
- **Tier 1 (Prohibitions - Unacceptable Risk)**: Article 5 (Cognitive behavioral manipulation, social scoring, biometric categorization for sensitive traits, predictive policing, emotion recognition in workplace/education, untargeted facial scraping, real-time RBI in public spaces).
- **Tier 2 (High-Risk Systems)**: Article 6(1) (Annex I harmonized products) & Article 6(2) (Annex III critical domains). Check Article 6(3) accessory derogation and mandatory profiling override.
- **Tier 3 (General-Purpose AI Models - GPAI)**: Article 51 (Systemic risk compute threshold $10^{25}$ FLOPs), Article 53 (Copyright policy, training summary), Article 55 (Systemic risk adversarial red-teaming, cybersecurity, incident reporting).
- **Tier 4 (Specific Transparency Risks)**: Article 50 (Direct interaction disclosure, synthetic audio/image/video watermarking, deep fake disclosure).

## 3. Defense & IHL Review Protocol
- Additional Protocol I Article 36 (mandatory legal review of new weapons, means, or methods of warfare).
- Core customary principles: Distinction (Art. 48/51), Proportionality (Art. 51(5)(b)), Precautions in attack (Art. 57), Prohibition of superfluous injury or unnecessary suffering (Art. 35(2)).
- UN CCW GGE 11 Guiding Principles on Lethal Autonomous Weapons Systems (LAWS).
